msgid "MicroProfile Fault Tolerance support"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus Tools for Visual Studio Code 1.4.0 has been released on the\n"
"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=redhat.vscode-quarkus[VS "
"Code Marketplace]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/redhat-developer/vscode-quarkus/[vscode-quarkus] 1.4.0 "
"fixes several bugs, including some performance issues, but the highlights of "
"this release revolve around bringing support for multiple MicroProfile "
"modules (Fault Tolerance, Health, LRA, Metrics, Open API, Open Tracing, Rest "
"Client), in both properties and Java files.\n"
"Many of these MicroProfile related enhancements were contributed by IBM."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For a list of all changes, please refer to the https://github.com/redhat-"
"developer/vscode-quarkus/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md[changelog]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Watch a demo video of all features presented in this article:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A little backstory on this release: it turns out, IBM had started to "
"implement its own https://github.com/MicroShed/microprofile-language-server/"
"[MicroProfile Language Server], providing MicroProfile support for https://"
"github.com/eclipse/microprofile-health[Health], Open API, Rest Client for "
"`Java files` (validation, quick fixes, completions). In the meantime, the "
"Red Hat's Quarkus Language Server had been refactored internally to split "
"the Quarkus related bits from a MicroProfile focused core. Naturally, Red "
"Hat and IBM realized there would be much value in contributing to a single "
"MicroProfile Language Server implementation, and both parties agreed to join "
"forces on developing the MicroProfile Language Server currently powering "
"https://github.com/redhat-developer/vscode-quarkus/[vscode-quarkus]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The outcome of this collaboration is the https://projects.eclipse.org/"
"proposals/eclipse-lsp4mp-language-server-eclipse-microprofile-0[Eclipse "
"LSP4MP (Language Server for Eclipse MicroProfile) project proposal]. So stay "
"tuned for more announcements on that subject!"
msgstr ""

msgid "And now for an overview of the new features in vscode-quarkus 1.4.0:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/eclipse/microprofile-fault-tolerance[MicroProfile Fault "
"Tolerance] properties are now managed in *.properties and yaml files, by "
"providing the correct properties, according to classes and methods annotated "
"with Fault Tolerance annotations:"
msgstr ""

msgid "MicroProfile Health support"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Validation and quick fixes for https://github.com/eclipse/microprofile-"
"health[MicroProfile Health] in Java files are now available:"
msgstr ""

msgid "MicroProfile LRA support"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/eclipse/microprofile-lra[MicroProfile LRA] (Long Running "
"Actions) properties are now supported in the *.properties and yaml files:"
msgstr ""

msgid "MicroProfile Metrics support"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/eclipse/microprofile-metrics[MicroProfile Metrics] "
"properties are now supported in the *.properties and yaml files:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In Java files, you benefit from snippets to quickly generate part of the "
"Metrics annotations:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"These Metrics snippets only appear if the Java project has MicroProfile "
"Metrics as a dependency."
msgstr ""

msgid "MicroProfile Open API support"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/eclipse/microprofile-open-api[MicroProfile Open API] "
"properties are now managed in *.properties and yaml files:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In Java files, you benefit from snippets to quickly generate part of the "
"Open API annotations:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"These Open API snippets only appear if the Java project depends on "
"MicroProfile Open API."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The code action `Sources... / Generate OpenAPI Annotations` provides the "
"ability to generate stub Open API annotations in a Java file:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The code action generates an Open API `@Operation` annotation for each "
"method that returns a response:"
msgstr ""

msgid "MicroProfile Open Tracing support"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/eclipse/microprofile-opentracing[MicroProfile Open "
"Tracing] properties are now managed in *.properties and yaml files:"
msgstr ""

msgid "MicroProfile Rest Client support"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Validation and quick fixes for https://github.com/eclipse/microprofile-rest-"
"client[MicroProfile Rest Client] in Java files are now available:"
msgstr ""

msgid "CodeLens for Rest Client are now available:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Moving Forward"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This wraps up the new major features in this release.\n"
"If you have any questions, suggestions or feedback, by all means please "
"https://github.com/redhat-developer/vscode-quarkus/issues/new[open a GitHub "
"issue]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For future releases we are aiming to improve language support for other "
"MicroProfile modules like MicroProfile Reactive Messaging and other new "
"Quarkus features like Command Mode Applications"
msgstr ""

msgid "Thank you for reading and stay tuned for the next release!"
msgstr ""

